      }

Again D[i][j] independent. So can parallelize.

Now also loops inside kernel have nested loops; we need to add pragma before outermost for.

Potential issue: In the first loop there is a reduction across k (tmp[i][j] += ...). But each iteration of i,j uses its own tmp element; the accumulation is a reduction on a scalar variable tmp[i][j] inside the innermost loop. Since each thread works on separate (i,j) element, no race; we can keep as is without reduction clause.

Thus add pragmas.

Also ensure not to break #pragma scop / #pragma endscop lines—they are PolyBench directives. We can still add OpenMP pragmas inside the region.

